  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support programme for victims of psychological suffering in Rwanda - CDJP Nyundo</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Its programme is centred around training on human rights, tolerance and reconciliation.  They integrated trauma aspects in its activities because of the observation it made on trauma during its interventions in the communities.

After building a pilot &#x201c;Peace House&#x201d;, the commission expect the use of this community infrastructure to attend its objectives and train people in trauma and other identified trainings that will contribute in trauma healing; peace and reconciliation and human rights and access to justice promotion. Counselling sessions, a variety of trainings (as for the other Justice and peace commission) and field visits are planned in 2008.</narrative>
  </description>
